NWOAS S161: normalize S102 guest RAM end / low-window backing across all consumers.

PROPOSED, NOT APPLIED.  Two steps from the apple_silicon_platforms_mu root:

  1. cp  nwoas_scripts/memory-s161/Include/Library/NwoasGuestRam.h \
         Silicon/Apple/AppleSiliconPkg/Include/Library/NwoasGuestRam.h
  2. git apply --check -p1 nwoas_scripts/memory-s161/nwoas-s161-guest-ram-normalize.diff
     git apply         -p1 nwoas_scripts/memory-s161/nwoas-s161-guest-ram-normalize.diff

(The new header is shipped as a file rather than embedded here so the review diff stays
tight; nothing in this diff compiles without it.)

Root cause (S158 log, S159 review): under NWOAS_WINDOW_AFTER_RAM=1 the hv already excludes
the 4 GiB window backing from boot_args.mem_size, but PrePi/AdtParser.c still subtracted
4 GiB (EARLY backing 0x9E0FCC000) and SetupApcieDarts() recomputed a local backing with an
unconditional minus-4 GiB, so the WIDE-DART L2 tables stopped at L1[1264] while the
ExitBootServices fill and NwoasHideHighRamDxe used phys_base+mem_size = 0xAE0FCC000.

Fix: one header-only helper (NwoasGuestRam.h) computes {GuestRamSize, GuestRamEnd,
BackingPa, BackingEnd} with overflow/underflow/alignment validation; all four consumers
call it.  Mode 1 subtracts nothing; legacy mode 0 subtracts exactly once.  The [0,4GiB)
window, NwoasHideHighRamDxe policy (NWOAS_HIDE_BASE, guard), and PCI leaf handling are
unchanged.  MemoryInitPeiLib's stale backing DEBUG range is corrected.

Line numbers are against the tree as read on 2026-09-10.

